WEBVTT

00:20.937 --> 00:23.064
huh?

00:24.691 --> 00:26.401
The fuck?
Who the hell are you?

00:35.827 --> 00:38.038
Come on. Come on, you son of a bitch.

00:38.663 --> 00:39.581
Asshole!

00:43.501 --> 00:44.794
Fuck this shit.

00:45.670 --> 00:46.504
Let's go.

00:48.131 --> 00:48.965
Oh…

00:52.802 --> 00:54.512
Bro, we gotta call an ambulance.

00:54.596 --> 00:57.057
That's a bad idea, Gun-woo.

00:57.140 --> 00:59.726
Dude, this guy is dying.

01:15.867 --> 01:16.868
Uh, Hyeon-ju,

01:16.951 --> 01:19.037
a homeless old man
was injured really badly,

01:19.120 --> 01:20.455
so we called an ambulance.

01:21.289 --> 01:24.501
- What about Yang Jae-myeong?
- Uh, he ran away.

01:24.584 --> 01:26.544
Goddammit! I told you not to get involved.

01:26.628 --> 01:28.588
I mean, he was really badly hurt.

01:28.671 --> 01:29.547
We had no choice.

01:29.631 --> 01:32.175
You don't even know the guy,
so why would you interfere? Damn it!

01:32.258 --> 01:34.677
Uh, I know, but we--

01:39.265 --> 01:40.183
So what should we do?

01:45.480 --> 01:46.439
I'll give her a call.

01:52.237 --> 01:54.030
What?

01:54.114 --> 01:58.243
Yes, Hyeon-ju, uh, about this…
We are really, really sorry.

01:58.326 --> 02:00.370
This was totally our fault 100 times over.

02:00.453 --> 02:03.081
Where are you right now?
Just let me apologize to you in person.

02:03.164 --> 02:04.958
Forget it. It's over.

02:05.500 --> 02:08.169
Please, Hyeon-ju,
just give us five minutes.

02:08.670 --> 02:12.048
We just… feel really badly,
and I'm sorry about the whole thing.

02:12.632 --> 02:14.467
Gun-woo also wants to apologize.

02:14.551 --> 02:16.803
Please, just give us five minutes.

02:17.387 --> 02:18.221
Come on.

02:18.721 --> 02:20.014
Meet me at the bookstore.

02:32.235 --> 02:33.278
Dude, look…

02:35.613 --> 02:37.365
To be honest with you,
I really don't get it.

02:37.448 --> 02:38.658
What don't you get, huh?

02:39.284 --> 02:41.161
I mean,
if we didn't do anything to help him,

02:41.244 --> 02:42.871
that old man would've definitely died.

02:42.954 --> 02:43.788
You saw it yourself.

02:44.372 --> 02:45.206
I did.

02:45.290 --> 02:47.208
So if saving that man was the right thing,

02:47.292 --> 02:49.043
why did you have to apologize
for what we did?

02:49.127 --> 02:52.130
- Why do we have to say we're sorry?
- This was our first time on the job.

02:52.630 --> 02:55.383
Hyeon-ju wasn't there, so it's hard
for her to understand what happened.

02:55.466 --> 02:57.343
She's still learning how we respond.

02:57.427 --> 02:59.554
That's why she got mad
when things didn't go as planned,

02:59.637 --> 03:02.765
but if we apologize and take the blame,
I think she'll be cool,

03:02.849 --> 03:04.684
and at the end,
hopefully she'll trust us more.

03:06.644 --> 03:08.646
- But…
- Gun-woo.

03:08.730 --> 03:11.774
I know you didn't do anything wrong.
I was right there with you.

03:11.858 --> 03:13.693
But thinking about it as a job,

03:14.402 --> 03:17.447
a new job with a new boss,
we should try to smooth it over.

03:18.448 --> 03:20.366
Just this once, okay?

03:22.410 --> 03:23.953
Yeah, okay.

03:48.978 --> 03:52.357
BLOODHOUNDS

04:00.365 --> 04:02.742
Don't sit. This won't take long.

04:03.451 --> 04:05.411
You fought Yang Jae-myeong, didn't you?

04:05.912 --> 04:07.914
We had no choice, so… so yeah.

04:07.997 --> 04:09.666
We can't work together anymore.

04:12.210 --> 04:14.837
What? Isn't it obvious?

04:15.421 --> 04:16.923
I mean, we said we were sorry.

04:17.006 --> 04:18.841
I don't need an apology!

04:20.426 --> 04:23.221
Yang Jae-myeong saw your faces, didn't he?

04:24.138 --> 04:25.932
My plan was to quietly tail him…

04:26.015 --> 04:26.849
…and gather evidence,

04:26.933 --> 04:29.435
but now that he knows someone's on to him,
he'll probably lie low,

04:29.519 --> 04:30.603
and who knows for long.

04:30.687 --> 04:33.439
So, because of you, my plan is ruined.

04:33.523 --> 04:35.900
We wore caps and masks.
He couldn't have seen our faces.

04:35.984 --> 04:39.529
Oh! You covered your face
then there's no way he can recognize you.

04:39.612 --> 04:42.198
Since this shitty hair was covered up,
you have an amazing disguise.

04:42.282 --> 04:44.659
Goddammit! I would recognize you
from a mile away!

04:44.742 --> 04:47.912
Well? Get out.

04:47.996 --> 04:49.247
- We apologized.
- I said get out!

04:49.330 --> 04:51.749
- We had no choice given the situation.
- What situation?

04:51.833 --> 04:53.293
It's our first time working together.

04:53.376 --> 04:55.253
- You can't expect perfection.
- That's why I refused you!

04:55.336 --> 04:57.839
- We did what we thought was right.
- What situation warrants that?

04:57.922 --> 04:59.257
- I told you earlier.
- Do you not hear me?

04:59.340 --> 05:02.010
- What does my hair have to do with it?
- We'll go. We'll go.

05:02.093 --> 05:03.886
We'll leave right now,
so please stop shouting.

05:05.888 --> 05:07.265
I will find a way to return

05:08.599 --> 05:10.768
the hundred million that Mr. Choi gave me.

05:12.812 --> 05:17.400
But… since Woo-jin and I just listened
to you yelling at us,

05:18.443 --> 05:20.028
please listen to one thing I have to say.

05:26.409 --> 05:28.870
If someone offered
to make your work go smoothly

05:30.747 --> 05:32.373
in exchange for killing someone,

05:33.458 --> 05:34.542
could you do it?

05:47.722 --> 05:49.724
That boss of Smile Capital
did this to my face.

05:51.851 --> 05:54.437
If I had done nothing
when a man was dying in front of me,

05:55.229 --> 05:57.857
then don't you think
I'd be even worse than that guy.

05:59.359 --> 06:00.777
It would have been wrong.

06:03.488 --> 06:04.864
Please just think about it.

06:40.274 --> 06:41.901
I'll find something else.

06:41.984 --> 06:43.111
Don't worry too much.

06:44.529 --> 06:46.781
I'm sorry. I couldn't hold myself back.

06:47.490 --> 06:49.367
You held back better than I did.

06:50.827 --> 06:53.746
You hungry?
I know this 24-hour soup place. Let's go.

06:55.540 --> 06:56.791
Wait.

06:58.042 --> 07:00.670
It's probably closed because of COVID.
It's past ten.

07:03.047 --> 07:05.258
Well that just made me hungry for nothing.

07:05.842 --> 07:06.717
I forgot.

07:09.762 --> 07:11.347
My stomach hurts.

07:12.932 --> 07:15.268
Hey, it isn't my fault they're closed
because of COVID.

07:16.310 --> 07:18.104
Well, it is your fault for bringing it up.

07:19.480 --> 07:22.358
Hey, you also couldn't hold yourself back
with her.

07:22.442 --> 07:24.277
You just said
I did a good job holding back.

07:24.360 --> 07:25.611
I only said it because I felt bad.

07:25.695 --> 07:28.489
- You were moping like a goddamn loser.
- I wasn't moping like a goddamn loser.

07:29.157 --> 07:32.827
"I wasn't moping
like a goddamn loser."

07:33.828 --> 07:34.954
What are you doing?

07:35.037 --> 07:38.040
I'm imitating you, you loser.
"God, I'm hungry."

07:38.124 --> 07:40.543
- "Oh, my stomach hurts."
- Wow.

07:40.626 --> 07:42.128
Dude, that's pretty harsh.

07:44.338 --> 07:45.923
You can't even take a joke now?

07:46.007 --> 07:48.551
Huh? You weren't joking.
That was totally serious.

07:49.635 --> 07:52.597
Hey, I'm seriously offended.
Apologize to me.

07:58.394 --> 08:01.314
SORRY, I WAS WRONG. SEE YOU AT THE OFFICE
TOMORROW AT 10:00 A.M.

08:05.026 --> 08:08.404
I knew this would happen.

08:51.364 --> 08:54.367
Yeah! It's short. It's short. It's short.

08:54.450 --> 08:55.451
- Super short.
- Super short!

08:55.535 --> 08:57.787
- Fuck! Will you shut the fuck up?
- Get out of here, loser.

08:57.870 --> 09:00.414
- "Will you shut the fuck up?"
- Why are you mad? It's just a game.

09:00.498 --> 09:01.999
- Calm down.
- It's your turn. Go!

09:02.083 --> 09:03.793
- Watch it.
- Okay, I will.

09:03.876 --> 09:05.670
- Your turn.
- Fuck off.

09:05.753 --> 09:06.712
YANG JAE-MYEONG
I'M WAITING IN FRONT OF THE GOLF SHOP

09:06.796 --> 09:07.630
Stop swearing.

09:07.713 --> 09:10.007
- You have to wear your mask, sir.
- Sure thing.

09:14.095 --> 09:15.137
What is it?

09:15.972 --> 09:18.099
Sir, someone was following us.

09:19.767 --> 09:20.643
Who was it?

09:21.352 --> 09:24.021
They were young,
but they seemed to know how to fight.

09:24.939 --> 09:25.773
Are you sure?

09:25.856 --> 09:26.691
Huh?

09:26.774 --> 09:28.651
You sure someone was following you,
you idiot?!

09:30.653 --> 09:31.529
Focus.

09:31.612 --> 09:32.613
Uh, the thing is…

09:33.823 --> 09:34.657
Talk.

09:35.324 --> 09:37.326
Before I started working for you, sir,

09:37.410 --> 09:38.911
I sort of borrowed money from a place.

09:38.995 --> 09:41.122
The fuckers didn't say anything,
so I just ignored them.

09:41.205 --> 09:42.290
Talk faster.

09:42.373 --> 09:44.500
But those guys
came for the money recently.

09:44.584 --> 09:47.587
The bastard that came over
was wearing a hat with a red cat on it.

09:47.670 --> 09:50.881
And one of the punks who jumped us
was wearing the same hat.

09:53.968 --> 09:55.052
You sure it's him?

09:56.804 --> 09:58.306
It was the same hat, sir.

10:02.852 --> 10:04.270
Where did you borrow the money from?

10:04.353 --> 10:06.856
So basically,
this is what happened yesterday.

10:07.523 --> 10:10.484
Yang Jae-myeong had already robbed
that homeless man of his ID,

10:10.568 --> 10:11.652
but he had forgotten,

10:11.736 --> 10:14.405
and he tried to con him again,
which ended up in a fight.

10:16.115 --> 10:18.075
Uh, but just how much money

10:18.159 --> 10:20.911
do Jae-myeong's guys borrow
with one stolen ID?

10:21.829 --> 10:23.748
About 50 million won per fake account.

10:24.415 --> 10:26.208
That's 500 million for ten IDs.

10:26.292 --> 10:28.461
Jesus. How long have they been doing this?

10:29.795 --> 10:31.797
I think at least for half a year, yeah.

10:31.881 --> 10:34.634
Wow! They must have made a small fortune.

10:35.134 --> 10:36.052
Hm.

10:36.135 --> 10:39.221
But those loan sharks that they conned,
did they just sit back and do nothing?

10:39.305 --> 10:41.098
If they call the cops,
they'll be investigated,

10:41.182 --> 10:42.350
so that's not an option.

10:42.433 --> 10:45.061
My take is they're trying to recover
the money on their own but can't.

10:47.521 --> 10:48.564
This is my plan.

10:48.648 --> 10:51.233
Find the private loan sharks
that Yang Jae-myeong conned,

10:51.317 --> 10:54.111
and then we recover the money he stole
for a commission.

10:55.446 --> 10:58.199
With a 1% commission,
we would get three billion won.

10:58.866 --> 10:59.992
We should at least charge 2%.

11:06.415 --> 11:07.249
Hyung?

11:08.709 --> 11:10.586
If loan sharks get conned,

11:10.670 --> 11:13.673
wouldn't that make things worse
for the people who got loans from them?

11:14.256 --> 11:15.383
Huh?

11:15.466 --> 11:18.469
They might end up torturing their clients
in order to get their money back.

11:19.220 --> 11:20.262
So what?

11:20.346 --> 11:24.433
It's just… I think small business owners
are the ones that will suffer the most.

11:25.601 --> 11:27.019
You're right about that.

11:27.103 --> 11:27.937
Mm.

11:40.783 --> 11:42.118
How did they find us?

11:42.952 --> 11:43.828
How did they find us?!

11:44.412 --> 11:45.329
I… I don't know.

11:48.582 --> 11:50.710
Turn off the lights and the sign outside.

11:51.377 --> 11:52.503
Damn it!

11:55.548 --> 11:57.800
PYEONGHWA BOOKS

11:59.135 --> 12:00.845
- Turn your phones off for now.
- Okay.

12:08.227 --> 12:10.479
- It's here? Are you sure?
- Yes. I'm sure, sir.

12:19.196 --> 12:21.282
You borrowed money from a bookstore?

12:21.365 --> 12:25.035
Yeah, the owner here used to be
a big moneylender back in the day.

12:41.927 --> 12:43.971
Hey, give this a kick here.

12:54.106 --> 12:54.982
Try this.

12:57.318 --> 12:58.986
Come on. Hurry up, you idiot.

13:00.321 --> 13:01.280
Ow.

13:06.160 --> 13:07.912
- Kick harder.
- Huh?

13:07.995 --> 13:09.622
Kick harder, you asshole!

13:09.705 --> 13:12.416
Uh…

13:12.500 --> 13:13.375
Harder!

13:14.418 --> 13:15.669
Harder!

13:15.753 --> 13:17.338
Kick fucking harder!

13:21.801 --> 13:23.886
Stop. That's enough.

13:23.969 --> 13:26.347
We'll need something stronger
to tear this down.

13:29.058 --> 13:30.392
This here is the safe.

14:10.182 --> 14:13.936
Last night on your way back,
did you check if you were being followed?

14:15.104 --> 14:17.356
Uh, well, we took the bus.

14:17.940 --> 14:20.150
You realize
they could have followed the bus.

14:20.234 --> 14:24.989
If they had followed us last night,
why didn't they jump us right away?

14:25.072 --> 14:26.657
Why decide to make their move now?

14:27.241 --> 14:30.119
- He might've wanted to bring Kim Jun-min--
- Whoa, no, Hyeon-ju.

14:30.202 --> 14:32.413
Yang Jae-myeong saw
how we fought last night.

14:32.496 --> 14:35.165
If he was planning on jumping us,
he would've brought more muscle.

14:35.749 --> 14:38.460
I bet…
they weren't sure.

14:38.961 --> 14:42.548
But now,
they might have caught onto something.

14:46.802 --> 14:50.514
In any case, we need to figure out
how they found out about this place.

14:50.598 --> 14:53.058
That's how
we don't make the same mistake twice

14:53.142 --> 14:54.685
Okay. That's a good idea.

14:54.768 --> 14:58.272
Why don't we sit down
and talk it through, hm?

14:59.064 --> 14:59.899
Hm.

15:05.779 --> 15:08.407
Does Yang Jae-myeong
know about this place?

15:09.074 --> 15:10.534
He came here a long time ago.

15:11.952 --> 15:16.123
That means he's caught onto
our connection here somehow.

15:16.624 --> 15:18.000
- Oh!
- Huh?

15:20.461 --> 15:21.587
Oh!

15:25.925 --> 15:26.759
Uh…

15:27.968 --> 15:30.179
Hyeon-ju, I think
he may have recognized your cap.

15:31.639 --> 15:33.807
The thing is,

15:33.891 --> 15:35.434
I followed you a while back

15:35.517 --> 15:37.645
when I saw you chasing down
a homeless man.

15:37.728 --> 15:38.812
Wait…

15:40.314 --> 15:42.983
Yeah, that was me.

15:43.567 --> 15:45.819
The homeless man back then
was Yang Jae-myeong.

15:46.403 --> 15:47.905
Oh, wow.

15:47.988 --> 15:51.450
Uh… I was wearing
that cap back then, wasn't I?

15:52.034 --> 15:54.787
Uh, yes,
I definitely remember seeing it on you.

15:56.330 --> 15:58.540
Then that might've been
how they found out.

15:58.624 --> 16:02.002
Okay, but why do you think
they kicked the shutters.

16:02.586 --> 16:05.881
Our shutters were custom-made
with steel, not aluminum.

16:05.965 --> 16:07.383
I think they were checking for that.

16:07.466 --> 16:09.885
I think they'll be back.

16:12.262 --> 16:13.305
Why is he here?

16:16.558 --> 16:17.601
Damn it.

16:31.031 --> 16:33.075
What have you done?

16:33.158 --> 16:34.994
That white car came here, didn't it?

16:36.578 --> 16:37.830
Are you not going to talk?

16:41.208 --> 16:43.794
I am sorry, sir. It's entirely my fault.

16:44.712 --> 16:47.840
The two of us…
We went on a job last night.

16:47.923 --> 16:49.091
What job?

16:49.174 --> 16:51.635
Uh, the thing is…

16:53.637 --> 16:54.513
What job was that?

16:56.557 --> 16:58.142
We were tailing Yang Jae-myeong.

16:59.268 --> 17:00.519
- Why?
- Grandpa.

17:00.602 --> 17:02.896
Loan sharks are desperate
to catch Yang Jae-myeong.

17:02.980 --> 17:05.107
I'm sure they'll be willing to pay for it.

17:05.941 --> 17:08.277
And I believe I'm the only one
who is able to catch him.

17:09.194 --> 17:10.529
Are you doing this to make money?

17:10.612 --> 17:12.364
It's good to make money.

17:14.116 --> 17:15.492
And what did you guys do?

17:16.493 --> 17:19.163
It's my… friends' job
to protect me, right?

17:19.747 --> 17:21.540
Well, they did.

17:22.875 --> 17:24.334
I'm disappointed in you.

17:26.295 --> 17:28.297
Yeah, well,
I'm disappointed in you too, Grandpa.

17:28.380 --> 17:30.507
It's clear Yang Jae-myeong
is up to no good,

17:30.591 --> 17:31.967
so why aren't you doing anything?

17:32.051 --> 17:35.512
With your orders, Mr. Hwang could
get rid of a loser like him immediately.

17:35.596 --> 17:38.474
So you're frustrated?
Well, I'm even more frustrated!

17:39.892 --> 17:42.644
Go ahead.
Take off that bandage on your face.

17:42.728 --> 17:44.480
- Hm?
- Hurry up and do it.

17:50.778 --> 17:53.906
If Yang Jae-myeong and Kim Jun-min
keep scamming private loan sharks,

17:54.740 --> 17:58.744
they'll keep threatening and harassing
powerless people like Gun-woo here.

17:59.369 --> 18:03.165
That's going to make
all the charity work you do meaningless.

18:03.248 --> 18:06.126
Your money will go straight
into their pockets!

18:06.794 --> 18:09.379
If you really want
to help out those in need,

18:09.463 --> 18:12.591
you should weed out the punks
like Yang Jae-myeong first.

18:14.468 --> 18:16.136
Who did that to Gun-woo's face?

18:18.889 --> 18:20.599
The boss of Smile Capital did it, sir.

18:22.142 --> 18:22.976
And his name?

18:23.936 --> 18:26.146
Uh, well, I don't know his name, sir.

18:26.939 --> 18:29.775
But he had a long knife scar
running down his left cheek.

18:38.951 --> 18:40.035
You guys head back now.

18:57.761 --> 19:01.640
Sir, could it just be a coincidence?

19:02.141 --> 19:05.519
Please check whether Kim Myeong-gil
is the CEO of Smile Capital.

19:06.019 --> 19:06.854
Yes, sir.

19:14.236 --> 19:16.280
Juju.

19:17.531 --> 19:20.659
- Getting too comfortable, aren't we?
- I mean, you called us friends before.

19:20.742 --> 19:22.911
I have to say, that felt good.

19:23.412 --> 19:24.413
So?

19:24.496 --> 19:27.958
So I thought it might be nice
to talk more casually with each other.

19:28.041 --> 19:30.043
We are a team, after all, Juju.

19:30.127 --> 19:32.671
Hm, we're not a team
if we don't speak casually?

19:32.754 --> 19:34.131
I'm just saying it would be nice

19:34.214 --> 19:35.841
if we acted more
like one big happy family.

19:35.924 --> 19:37.176
It's just a suggestion.

19:37.259 --> 19:40.929
Well, if we're family,
the oldest would treat the rest to a meal.

19:41.013 --> 19:42.139
So will you be buying?

19:42.764 --> 19:45.058
Uh, I actually prefer formalities, ma'am.

19:45.142 --> 19:46.810
I'm kidding. Relax.

19:46.894 --> 19:49.146
Let's use Grandpa's credit card.
What do you guys want?

19:49.229 --> 19:50.063
Rib eye.

19:50.772 --> 19:51.607
Then you pay.

19:53.066 --> 19:54.318
Uh, barbecue buffet.

19:54.401 --> 19:57.487
- A barbecue buffet?
- Yeah, I know a really great place.

20:01.116 --> 20:02.618
Mm, sure.

20:02.701 --> 20:03.535
Let's go!

20:06.788 --> 20:09.041
How long have you been friends
with Gun-woo?

20:10.000 --> 20:13.295
I don't think it really matters
how long you've known a person.

20:13.378 --> 20:16.131
Just knowing someone for a while
doesn't mean they're your friend.

20:16.215 --> 20:17.049
Okay.

20:17.132 --> 20:21.803
What really matters is how similar
your life trajectories have been.

20:21.887 --> 20:23.805
So even if it's a short conversation,

20:23.889 --> 20:25.891
you gain a deep understanding
of each other.

20:25.974 --> 20:27.434
That's what matters.

20:27.517 --> 20:29.686
- That's the relationship you guys have?
- Right.

20:29.770 --> 20:31.563
It's like we're boxers,

20:31.647 --> 20:34.441
but we exchange a lot more
than just our fists. Pow!

20:35.025 --> 20:37.027
"So that's the kind of life you've lived."

20:37.110 --> 20:37.945
Pow!

20:38.028 --> 20:39.571
"Well, this is how I lived, you punk."

20:39.655 --> 20:45.327
Each blow contains
both fighters' character, heart,

20:45.410 --> 20:48.538
history, history,

20:49.289 --> 20:50.165
History?

20:50.791 --> 20:51.959
History.

20:53.252 --> 20:54.753
We see it all.

20:54.836 --> 20:55.921
We know. Mm.

20:56.797 --> 20:57.631
Sure.

20:57.714 --> 20:59.591
And besides, Gun-woo is…

21:01.593 --> 21:02.928
a senior Marine.

21:04.263 --> 21:06.056
And that tells you everything.

21:06.723 --> 21:08.267
What exactly does it tell you?

21:10.060 --> 21:11.186
Everything.

21:11.270 --> 21:12.479
Everything about what?

21:12.562 --> 21:15.649
Juju, this isn't something
I just can't easily explain to you.

21:15.732 --> 21:17.359
It's just, you know, a Marine thing.

21:17.442 --> 21:21.280
It's like when rappers use hip-hop
as an all-encompassing term

21:21.363 --> 21:23.699
when they look at something
and go, "This is hip-hop."

21:23.782 --> 21:25.325
It's indescribable.

21:25.409 --> 21:27.953
Oh, indescribable, you say?

21:28.745 --> 21:31.039
- Are you being sarcastic?
- Who? Me?

21:31.123 --> 21:32.457
Hey, this stuff is really…

21:32.541 --> 21:33.667
- Here we go.
- Right.

21:37.879 --> 21:38.714
Huh?

21:39.506 --> 21:41.967
Dude,
you haven't turned on the grill yet?

21:42.050 --> 21:43.218
You didn't tell me to.

21:43.302 --> 21:46.013
Come on, man. Whoever is sitting down
is supposed to get the grill going.

21:46.096 --> 21:48.390
I didn't know that.
Why didn't you turn it when we got here?

21:48.473 --> 21:51.560
Because the grill would've burned up
in the time it took to return with meat.

21:51.643 --> 21:53.353
How would a grill burn up?

21:53.437 --> 21:56.690
Well, technically,
the grill itself doesn't burn.

21:56.773 --> 21:58.984
The meat would burn
the second you place it on the grill.

21:59.067 --> 22:00.193
You're talking about meat burning?

22:00.277 --> 22:02.487
That's what people mean
when they say they're burning the grill.

22:02.571 --> 22:05.782
Well, that's insider lingo for people
who work at barbecue restaurants.

22:05.866 --> 22:07.784
My mom also refers to it
as "burning the grill."

22:07.868 --> 22:09.745
Well, my mom doesn't.

22:10.329 --> 22:12.122
- For someone who knows meat--
- There!

22:12.748 --> 22:13.749
Get grilling.

22:13.832 --> 22:15.208
Uh, no.

22:15.292 --> 22:18.170
It's too soon for the meat.
Can't put it on a lukewarm grill.

22:18.253 --> 22:19.880
That would ruin the flavor.
You gotta wait.

22:22.841 --> 22:25.218
Shall we maybe converse
while the grill is heating up?

22:26.136 --> 22:29.556
Gun-woo, just speak naturally for once.

22:29.639 --> 22:31.433
Uh, so are you and Mr. Choi related?

22:32.017 --> 22:34.644
Huh? Well, that came out of left field.

22:34.728 --> 22:36.188
I've wanted to know too.

22:36.271 --> 22:37.939
Since the very beginning, Juju.

22:39.858 --> 22:40.692
Well…

22:41.943 --> 22:43.528
…long story short…

22:46.156 --> 22:48.575
I was diagnosed with spinal cancer
when I was eight.

22:49.743 --> 22:51.536
I was cured by the time I was ten,

22:53.789 --> 22:56.041
but then… my dad died.

22:57.209 --> 22:59.836
So I was sent to an orphanage,

23:01.213 --> 23:03.173
I hated it so much that I ran away.

23:04.341 --> 23:06.134
I used to get so hungry, you know,

23:07.177 --> 23:10.764
that I ate leftover jjajangmyeon
that people left on their doorstep.

23:11.515 --> 23:13.767
I also worked at bars
with other runaway kids,

23:15.018 --> 23:16.645
but I couldn't do it anymore.

23:18.480 --> 23:20.065
So I returned to the orphanage.

23:22.317 --> 23:25.570
But I was then dragged off
to a different orphanage when I was 17.

23:26.488 --> 23:28.407
And Grandpa happened to be
the owner there.

23:28.490 --> 23:30.367
- You mean Mr. Choi?
- Yes.

23:31.368 --> 23:34.246
He said he built an orphanage
because he wanted to do something good.

23:36.164 --> 23:38.208
He was really nice to me in particular.

23:38.834 --> 23:40.794
So at first,
I thought he might be a pervert, but…

23:42.796 --> 23:44.297
I came to know as time passed…

23:46.466 --> 23:48.135
that he was being sincere.

23:48.218 --> 23:50.762
Grandpa paid for me
to learn everything I know now.

23:50.846 --> 23:52.305
because I didn't have the money.

23:52.389 --> 23:56.143
I learned kendo, how to ride a motorcycle.

24:02.023 --> 24:04.818
I could tell immediately
that Mr. Choi is really a nice person.

24:05.527 --> 24:06.820
Since middle school,

24:06.903 --> 24:09.948
I've been working part-time jobs
to pay off my dad's debt.

24:10.031 --> 24:12.701
But when our debt got to 100 million won,

24:12.784 --> 24:14.453
I suddenly felt totally helpless.

24:15.412 --> 24:18.248
So I know how scary
a hundred million won can be.

24:18.748 --> 24:21.918
And when Mr. Choi gave me that money,
telling me to pay off my debts,

24:22.002 --> 24:23.253
I thought to myself,

24:24.337 --> 24:26.965
I have to make sure to protect this man
at all costs.

24:29.176 --> 24:32.804
Grandpa told me that
in order to judge someone's character,

24:32.888 --> 24:34.473
one should open up your heart.

24:34.556 --> 24:37.100
That people with character
will see your sincerity

24:37.184 --> 24:38.185
and return it in kind,

24:38.977 --> 24:41.396
and those who lack depth
will try to use that against you.

24:42.647 --> 24:44.649
- Agreed.
- You're a nice person, Gun-woo.

24:45.275 --> 24:49.196
Thanks. Two things I'm good at
are being nice and being diligent.

24:49.821 --> 24:51.698
- I think we can start grilling now.
- Mm-hm.

24:58.914 --> 25:00.540
Ah!

25:00.624 --> 25:04.169
- Ah, perfect timing. Very nice.
- You're getting pretty good at this.

25:04.252 --> 25:06.379
Well, I mean,
I learned from the best, right?

25:07.005 --> 25:09.466
Wow, I'm feeling so left out
all of a sudden.

25:10.342 --> 25:11.843
Sheesh, never mind.

25:11.927 --> 25:12.761
Hurry up and flip it.

25:12.844 --> 25:15.222
- I can't do that yet.
- You gotta trust him. He's good at this.

25:15.305 --> 25:17.974
Sorry,
I didn't know he was the grill master.

25:18.058 --> 25:19.184
You will soon.

25:21.311 --> 25:23.104
Smells amazing!

25:23.605 --> 25:24.856
Oh!

25:25.357 --> 25:26.399
Let's clean out the buffet.

25:26.483 --> 25:27.484
Sure.

25:28.068 --> 25:30.237
- When are those stitches coming off?
- Tomorrow morning.

25:30.320 --> 25:31.321
Does it hurt?

25:31.404 --> 25:32.906
Not too bad.

25:33.949 --> 25:37.160
- I asked for mine hot.
- You're supposed to take your coffee cold.

25:37.244 --> 25:38.954
Seriously? Come on.

25:39.579 --> 25:40.747
- Hyeon-ju.
- Yeah?

25:40.830 --> 25:42.666
Yang Jae-myeong knows
where the bookstore is.

25:42.749 --> 25:44.292
Shouldn't we do something about it?

25:45.669 --> 25:47.671
I'll talk it over with Grandpa.

25:48.213 --> 25:50.882
You should ask him soon.
We don't have time.

25:50.966 --> 25:51.800
Okay.

25:53.677 --> 25:54.636
Ms. Lee.

25:55.136 --> 25:57.389
The lobby is a hotel's first impression.

25:57.472 --> 25:59.224
I want us to impress
our international guests

25:59.307 --> 26:01.476
with the most beautiful,
stunning Korean experience

26:01.560 --> 26:02.561
they've ever encountered.

26:02.644 --> 26:04.396
Something
they've never experienced before.

26:04.479 --> 26:05.438
That kind of thing.

26:05.522 --> 26:06.731
Yes, I understand.

26:06.815 --> 26:07.857
TEAM LEADER LEE SO-HYEON

26:07.941 --> 26:10.652
Anyway, I look forward to hearing
your brilliant ideas.

26:10.735 --> 26:12.112
See you tomorrow morning.

26:12.195 --> 26:14.656
Our casino will be
on the top floor of that hotel.

26:14.739 --> 26:19.160
My goal is a hundred billion
in annual revenue.

26:19.244 --> 26:20.870
There are a lot of people
itching for a fix

26:20.954 --> 26:24.249
now that gambling in Macau
has been blocked off due to COVID.

26:24.833 --> 26:29.296
We'll secretly book them a suite
every week and let them have fun

26:30.297 --> 26:32.716
while secretly catching their gambling
on camera.

26:32.799 --> 26:35.510
Afterward, once we have enough cash,

26:36.177 --> 26:39.681
Jang-do will make sure
to hand over to the police

26:40.348 --> 26:41.891
all evidence of gambling.

26:43.643 --> 26:46.146
When the hotel is ruined
and worth nothing,

26:47.105 --> 26:50.942
we'll swoop in
and take over the whole thing.

26:57.741 --> 27:00.076
We need to be ready
to spend a hundred billion

27:00.160 --> 27:02.871
by the time Jang-do returns
with dirt on Director Hong.

27:03.371 --> 27:06.124
We're 50 billion short, right?

27:06.207 --> 27:07.042
Yes.

27:08.752 --> 27:10.712
Now it's time to collect on everything.

27:11.921 --> 27:14.424
Sell off anything that's of any value.

27:16.134 --> 27:17.552
Coming through!

27:24.351 --> 27:25.310
Yes, sir.

27:25.393 --> 27:27.896
Yes, that car you mentioned before
just came in.

27:27.979 --> 27:29.147
Cool.

27:30.482 --> 27:31.900
I'll be right back, sir.

27:43.787 --> 27:45.038
What the…

27:51.378 --> 27:52.212
CAR WASH EXIT
NO PARKING

27:53.421 --> 27:54.255
Hello!

27:56.257 --> 27:58.134
Damn it.

28:12.732 --> 28:15.318
All right, keep him down.

28:18.863 --> 28:20.073
Look at him!

28:26.329 --> 28:27.539
You want more, huh?

28:28.123 --> 28:30.291
Grab him.

28:35.588 --> 28:37.298
Hey, strip him down.

28:46.474 --> 28:47.308
Ah.

28:48.059 --> 28:49.811
- He's this way.
- Is he in there now?

28:49.894 --> 28:51.771
- Yes.
- Thank you for your hard work.

28:54.149 --> 28:56.151
- You can count it.
- Thank you, sir.

28:56.234 --> 28:58.403
Look at him.

29:02.699 --> 29:03.742
Hey. Hey, shh.

29:03.825 --> 29:05.744
Whoa!
You boys sure did a number on him.

29:05.827 --> 29:07.036
- Hello, sir!
- Hello, sir!

29:07.120 --> 29:08.163
I'm so cold.

29:08.246 --> 29:10.540
Can I please have
something to wear? Please.

29:10.623 --> 29:11.666
God, I'm… I'm sorry, sir.

29:16.546 --> 29:17.464
Hi there.

29:21.217 --> 29:23.678
You…

29:23.762 --> 29:25.889
You, it's you, isn't it? Fuck.

29:25.972 --> 29:27.140
Motherfucker!

29:28.516 --> 29:31.269
Jesus, not too long ago,
you were acting like hot shit.

29:32.645 --> 29:33.480
Prick.

29:34.147 --> 29:34.981
So,

29:36.024 --> 29:38.651
you really shouldn't have fucked around
with him.

29:39.277 --> 29:41.446
Did you think he would get scared

29:41.529 --> 29:46.242
and apologize to you or something
just because your cousin's a cop? Huh?

29:54.959 --> 29:58.797
Listen, let me teach you a little lesson.

29:58.880 --> 30:02.884
Wild animals bite back if you hit them.

30:04.594 --> 30:08.014
It doesn't matter how much stronger
or weaker you are than them.

30:08.807 --> 30:10.350
They just bite back.

30:19.025 --> 30:20.318
Now then.

30:23.404 --> 30:24.239
Strip down.

30:24.322 --> 30:25.490
What?

30:25.573 --> 30:27.784
Come on, take everything off,
including your underwear.

30:27.867 --> 30:31.538
No, I get it now.
Please, just this once.

30:31.621 --> 30:33.122
- Ugh.
- I'm sorry.

30:33.206 --> 30:35.542
I really don't know what this is about,
but I'm really sorry.

30:35.625 --> 30:36.501
Hey, In-beom.

30:36.584 --> 30:38.711
Please, just this once.

30:43.341 --> 30:44.551
Wrap it up.

30:55.562 --> 30:56.729
Are you stripping or not?

30:58.773 --> 31:00.149
Don't kill me.

31:00.942 --> 31:03.486
I guess you're still thirsty.

31:06.823 --> 31:09.075
- Oh!
- What's it gonna be?

31:17.959 --> 31:20.169
- Well…
- I'll strip down! I'll strip down!

31:26.885 --> 31:28.344
Good call.

31:28.428 --> 31:30.388
Now then, Director Hong,
without further ado,

31:30.471 --> 31:31.598
let's see you strip.

31:49.198 --> 31:50.533
I GOT SOMETHING BIG

31:50.617 --> 31:52.702
All right, that's enough.

32:28.988 --> 32:29.906
Yes.

32:29.989 --> 32:31.741
Uh, Mr. Choi,

32:31.824 --> 32:36.037
the Kim Myeong-gil we know
is indeed the CEO of Smile Capital.

32:36.704 --> 32:38.081
Yes, I understand.

32:38.957 --> 32:41.584
I'm coming to pick you up.
I'll be there soon, sir.

32:42.085 --> 32:43.836
Yes.

33:04.732 --> 33:06.526
I apologize for my sudden decision.

33:09.570 --> 33:12.323
Recently, I've gone through
something very difficult for me.

33:14.325 --> 33:16.744
And I came to this conclusion
after thinking things over,

33:16.828 --> 33:18.246
so I hope you'll understand.

33:19.205 --> 33:21.833
Our company will be terminated
by the end of the month.

33:23.584 --> 33:25.086
I will be wiring you

33:25.837 --> 33:28.381
all of your salary
as well as your severance pay.

33:32.468 --> 33:33.594
Thanks for everything.

33:34.554 --> 33:39.642
Sir, what about… all of our money
that's out there right now?

33:40.518 --> 33:41.853
I'm gonna take care of it.

34:08.713 --> 34:10.506
Papa!

34:31.319 --> 34:33.863
- Yes.
- This is Oh In-muk in security, sir.

34:34.447 --> 34:36.491
Some robbers have broken into your office.

34:37.366 --> 34:38.367
How many?

34:43.748 --> 34:45.208
I think there are two.

35:10.817 --> 35:11.734
Hey!

35:13.319 --> 35:14.403
What's taking you so long?

35:15.363 --> 35:18.491
This model normally comes
with a six-digit combination.

35:18.574 --> 35:19.534
This one has eight.

35:19.617 --> 35:20.993
I think they modified it.

35:22.370 --> 35:24.622
- What does that mean?
- Gonna need more time.

35:25.373 --> 35:26.374
Hurry it up.

35:51.107 --> 35:51.941
Got it!

35:53.526 --> 35:54.777
Out of the way.

36:03.536 --> 36:04.787
PRIVATE LOAN STANDARD AGREEMENT

36:04.871 --> 36:08.082
These promissory notes
are worth a billion won a pop.

36:08.166 --> 36:09.125
Fuck!

36:28.144 --> 36:30.646
No one has come out.
I also held the elevator here.

36:30.730 --> 36:31.898
Thank you.

36:32.481 --> 36:35.276
Uh, shall I accompany you?

36:35.359 --> 36:38.196
Oh, no. I'll be fine. Thank you very much.

36:38.988 --> 36:41.115
Uh, let me just borrow this.

36:41.199 --> 36:42.033
Sure.

37:17.902 --> 37:18.986
Who are you?

37:23.032 --> 37:24.158
How did you get in?

38:19.672 --> 38:20.715
Who sent you?

38:25.261 --> 38:29.223
Who sent you?

38:29.307 --> 38:32.435
Who sent you?

38:35.688 --> 38:36.856
Who sent you?

38:38.107 --> 38:39.775
Who sent you?

39:00.004 --> 39:01.297
Fuck.

40:34.098 --> 40:35.391
Sir, are you okay?

40:35.474 --> 40:36.725
Kill that fucker!

41:25.733 --> 41:27.109
It's okay, Beom. Huh?

41:27.193 --> 41:29.195
- Snap out of it. You're okay.
- Okay.

41:29.278 --> 41:30.529
Yes, sir.

41:30.613 --> 41:32.156
- Kang In-beom!
- Yes, sir!

41:34.074 --> 41:35.201
We don't have time.

41:35.826 --> 41:38.245
Take all the money in the safe
and head down first, okay?

41:43.083 --> 41:45.169
Calm down. Calm down.

42:15.699 --> 42:16.617
Huh?

42:17.284 --> 42:18.244
Sir!

42:19.495 --> 42:20.829
He's not there!

42:26.001 --> 42:27.503
- Just go downstairs.
- Yes, sir.

42:49.275 --> 42:50.943
- Mr. Choi.
- Hm?

43:20.889 --> 43:22.641
Have you thought about it yet?

43:26.937 --> 43:28.355
What's the problem?

43:29.690 --> 43:31.233
Let's avoid Yang Jae-myeong.

43:32.151 --> 43:32.985
Why?

43:33.694 --> 43:35.654
Those people also resort to killing.

43:35.738 --> 43:37.615
I want to move the bookstore as well.

43:37.698 --> 43:39.241
Why?

43:39.325 --> 43:40.284
Hyeon-ju.

43:43.662 --> 43:44.496
Look at me.

43:48.626 --> 43:50.586
I am old and tired.

43:51.170 --> 43:53.380
There's no strength or courage left in me

43:54.632 --> 43:55.716
to fight them.

43:56.216 --> 43:58.844
I just want to live
my remaining days in peace,

43:59.511 --> 44:01.680
teaching you the things
I want to teach you,

44:02.765 --> 44:04.516
and giving you all the things that…

44:06.560 --> 44:09.229
that I want to leave to you
once I'm not here anymore.

44:11.148 --> 44:13.150
That is the only thing I want right now.

44:18.072 --> 44:19.907
Do you understand what I'm saying?

44:25.579 --> 44:26.664
Good.

44:28.040 --> 44:29.083
And thank you.

45:52.332 --> 45:54.168
Remember, the value of gold rises

45:54.710 --> 45:58.839
every single time people lose confidence
in fiat currency.

45:59.548 --> 46:01.258
You gotta your slush fund in gold.

46:02.009 --> 46:05.471
Besides, if you melt the gold down
and mix it with other gold,

46:05.554 --> 46:06.638
it launders itself.

46:07.931 --> 46:10.350
That was the very first thing I learned
when I worked for Choi.

46:14.354 --> 46:16.523
Failing to get my hands
on his hidden gold…

46:18.984 --> 46:20.819
is something that I still regret.

46:21.528 --> 46:23.071
That old stupid fuck.

46:24.239 --> 46:27.618
He suddenly grows a conscience
and closes down the damn company.

47:20.087 --> 47:22.172
- Beom.
- Yes, sir.

47:22.965 --> 47:24.091
Get in here.

47:35.435 --> 47:36.395
What do you think?

47:36.937 --> 47:38.522
It's amazing.

47:43.694 --> 47:45.654
Each bar is worth 500 million.

47:45.737 --> 47:47.573
If our business in Korea goes south,

47:48.866 --> 47:51.743
you and I will take all this gold
and go to Vietnam.

47:51.827 --> 47:52.870
Huh?

47:52.953 --> 47:54.037
We can hide there.

47:54.121 --> 47:56.623
I planted someone
in the Vietnamese government.

47:58.000 --> 47:58.834
Thanks to this,

48:00.460 --> 48:03.463
we should be able to live like kings
for the rest of our days.

48:05.799 --> 48:06.758
Thank you, sir. I…

48:11.722 --> 48:13.515
You're a brother to me.

48:14.099 --> 48:15.726
I would do anything for you.

48:17.477 --> 48:18.312
Beom, listen.

48:20.856 --> 48:23.942
Out here, you are all I've got.

48:25.527 --> 48:26.612
You know that, right?

48:27.654 --> 48:28.530
Mm-hm.

48:34.119 --> 48:36.413
Come on.

48:36.496 --> 48:38.790
It's the best
stir-fried spicy pork in the world.

48:38.874 --> 48:40.542
- It's that good?
- Yeah.

48:50.218 --> 48:51.970
Auntie? Auntie!

48:53.347 --> 48:55.807
Auntie. Auntie.

48:56.350 --> 48:58.185
It's okay. It's okay. It's me, Woo-jin.

48:58.268 --> 49:01.313
Oh God, Woo-jin.
Woo-jin, Woo-jin.

49:02.064 --> 49:03.315
What happened?

49:04.191 --> 49:06.777
I… I took out a private loan.

49:07.486 --> 49:08.987
They told me to pay them back.

49:09.071 --> 49:12.532
I told them I had no money
because I didn't get any customers today.

49:12.616 --> 49:14.993
And they smashed everything.

49:15.077 --> 49:17.704
God, I'm scared. I'm so scared.

49:18.997 --> 49:20.582
What do I do?

49:26.380 --> 49:29.216
How is she supposed to
operate her business if you smash it up?

49:29.299 --> 49:31.093
How do you expect her to pay you back now?

49:31.593 --> 49:33.345
She wasn't paying.
What should I do?

49:33.428 --> 49:35.722
You should ease up on them.
Everyone's having a tough time.

49:35.806 --> 49:37.766
And how am I supposed to make a living?

49:37.849 --> 49:39.935
You know what, why don't you pay for her?

49:40.519 --> 49:43.522
Come on,
you know I don't have the money for that.

49:43.605 --> 49:45.232
Then just shut your goddamn mouth.

49:45.315 --> 49:47.109
And mind your own fucking business.

49:47.901 --> 49:49.736
- Got it?
- Fine.

49:59.371 --> 50:00.247
It's Im.

50:01.665 --> 50:03.166
I worked with him back in the day.

50:03.250 --> 50:06.128
Apparently, he just got conned
by someone he lent 500 million to.

50:06.211 --> 50:08.046
- Is Yang Jae-myeong involved?
- I don't know.

50:08.130 --> 50:10.257
I didn't ask for the details.

50:10.340 --> 50:13.552
But it was a homeless person's ID
that they used to open a fake account.

50:13.635 --> 50:14.553
Identical MO.

50:15.137 --> 50:16.096
It's him.

50:17.431 --> 50:18.432
I say we should catch him.

50:20.642 --> 50:22.561
I can't just stand by
and do nothing about it.

50:23.145 --> 50:24.980
Grandpa told us to lie low.

50:25.856 --> 50:27.232
That they're really dangerous.

50:27.315 --> 50:29.568
But I think it's wrong to do nothing
after seeing all that.

50:30.152 --> 50:32.487
What if I call him back
and tip him off about Yang Jae-myeong,

50:32.571 --> 50:33.655
so he can catch him himself.

50:34.781 --> 50:36.908
If the goal is to capture him,
we should do it.

50:37.409 --> 50:38.618
Maybe we could make some money.

50:38.702 --> 50:42.330
If we do make money from this,
can I use it to help out Auntie?

50:42.414 --> 50:45.417
If we do, we'll split it evenly.
Feel free to use it however you see fit.

50:46.668 --> 50:49.296
- Cool.
- Then I want to help her too.

50:53.133 --> 50:54.051
Come here.

50:57.804 --> 50:59.556
- Come on over.
- No.

51:02.684 --> 51:03.602
Thank you.

51:18.075 --> 51:18.909
All in.

51:32.047 --> 51:34.466
Sir, you should look at this.

51:37.010 --> 51:38.428
That car over there.

51:39.554 --> 51:41.932
They cut the engine,
but no one's getting out.

51:44.851 --> 51:46.186
- Hey, get ready.
- Yes, sir.

51:47.479 --> 51:48.897
Hey, check your phone.

51:48.980 --> 51:50.107
- Yes, sir.
- Okay, okay.

51:56.863 --> 51:58.240
Hey, sir, they're here.

51:58.740 --> 52:02.077
In exactly two hours, make your move.

52:26.143 --> 52:27.144
They're here.

52:35.569 --> 52:36.528
Let's go. Let's go.

52:42.576 --> 52:44.619
You're gonna die today, you dumb fucks.

53:50.310 --> 53:51.186
Yes, sir.

53:52.229 --> 53:53.355
Come down now.

54:03.490 --> 54:04.574
Come out!

54:05.492 --> 54:08.995
Hey, you fuckers, I know you're there,
so hurry up and show yourselves.

54:09.079 --> 54:11.831
Come out, assholes!
What is this, hide-and-seek?

54:12.666 --> 54:13.541
Motherfuckers.

54:27.806 --> 54:28.640
Please pick up…

54:29.432 --> 54:30.267
Please.

54:30.350 --> 54:32.227
HYEON-JU

54:37.315 --> 54:38.608
- Mm?
- Grandpa.

54:38.692 --> 54:40.068
Woo-jin and Gun-woo are in danger.

54:41.152 --> 54:42.237
Where are you?

54:42.320 --> 54:44.531
- Get a move on.
- Let's go! Let's go!

54:44.614 --> 54:46.032
You sons of bitches!

54:46.116 --> 54:48.285
- Let's get 'em.
- Fuck.

54:49.703 --> 54:52.080
- Get a move on.
- Go, go, go!

54:53.540 --> 54:55.959
Oh, fuck. This is insane.

54:57.502 --> 54:59.045
Hey, you sons of bitches.
